  "description": "Native AOT, ultra-fast, strictly typed, and memory-efficient Excel (.xlsx) reader/writer for .NET. 100% Native AOT compatible with zero reflection.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "ExcelFlow",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-15T14:50:55.857Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "FG45fG8QL76+0EaD7svrTrmzxZ9iWmJmsuhUhrLVAdtgZQ0ywVTUR955CsbtPOcGg29CBl/u6bmS3dCqEFnboQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 86703,
  "published": "2026-07-15T14:47:45.887Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0\n- FIX: the source generator is now packed into the NuGet package (analyzers/dotnet/cs); previously consumers of the package did not receive generated mappers.\n- FIX: reading no longer throws NullReferenceException when a header cell is empty.\n- FIX: ExcelParseError.RowNumber now reports the real 1-based sheet row when SkipRows() is used.\n- FIX: DateTime values parsed from strings now use InvariantCulture (was CurrentCulture).\n- FIX: written DateTime cells now carry a date number format and display as dates in Excel (was raw OADate numbers).\n- FIX: nullable numeric/date properties (e.g. decimal?) no longer break the generated writer.\n- CHANGE: Excel.Read(Stream) no longer disposes the caller's stream; pass leaveOpen: false to opt into the old behavior.\n- CHANGE: OnError() can now be called multiple times; all handlers are invoked.\n- NEW: Guid and enum properties are supported natively.\n- NEW: compile-time diagnostics: EXF001 (class must be partial), EXF002 (unsupported property type), EXF003 (generic classes not supported).\n- NEW: files opened by path are opened with FileShare.Read, so a file open in Excel can still be read.",
